/* No `display: none` here (deliberately, see this file's own module docstring): a
`display: none` child reserves zero layout space, which used to let `FindingsDescription`'s
sibling `width: 1fr` silently expand to fill the whole row whenever this column had
nothing to show. `FindingsSuggestion` now always occupies its `1fr` column -- only the
border (drawn below, `.-visible` only) and this widget's own text content are what
actually toggle with highlight state. */
FindingsSuggestion {
    width: 1fr;
    padding: 0 1;
    height: auto;
}

FindingsSuggestion.-visible {
    border: round $border-color-muted;
}

FindingsSuggestion Input {
    border: none !important;
    height: 1 !important;
    padding: 0 1;
}

FindingsSuggestion .-chat-hint {
    color: $fg-muted;
    height: 1;
    padding: 0 1;
}

/* "Chat about it" (`self._custom`, `_CUSTOM_ENTRY`) should read as "type your own", not as
another agent-generated suggestion -- `$fg-secondary` (also used by `FindingBox`'s own
`.footer-hint`, `finding.tcss`) is the lighter, more-visible-than-`$fg-muted` gray of
this theme's two dim text tokens, and staying off `$fg-muted` keeps this entry visually
distinct from `.-chat-hint`'s own dimmer reminder line above. */
FindingsSuggestion .-custom-entry {
    color: $fg-secondary;
}

/* A real horizontal divider directly above "Chat about it", replacing the blank line that
used to appear there (that gap was actually a stray trailing `Text` newline from
`render_decision_cycle_head`'s entries, not a CSS margin -- see that function's own
docstring). Reuses this column's own border color (`$border-color-muted`, `.-visible`
above) so the divider reads as an internal continuation of this box's own border. Only
applied while `-decision` is present -- toggled on in `show_decision`, off in
`show_plain`/`clear` -- so plain mode and a hidden/cleared column never show a divider
above nothing. */
FindingsSuggestion .-custom-entry.-decision {
    border-top: solid $border-color-muted;
}
